# function plus(list) { let total = 0; for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) total += list[i]; return total; }      sink(plus);
# Nothing is known of `list`, so the loop is built by kinds: a copy for a list of numbers, one for any list, one for bytes, one for the other views, and the loop as written.
# Whoever chooses the copy for a list of numbers asks the list for storage that holds numbers alone. The front of that copy asked the same question of the same cell once more, with nothing in between that writes:
# five instructions at each entry. An equal question that has been answered on the way is found again, as an equal comparison is.
